\title{scMaSigPro: Differential Expression Analysis Along Single-Cell Trajectories}
\description{
scMaSigPro finds genes whose expression changes along pseudotime and
differs between the branching paths of a single-cell trajectory. The
cells of each path are pseudo-bulked into pseudotime bins, and the
polynomial generalised linear model of maSigPro is fitted to the binned
counts, by default with a negative binomial family and size-factor
offsets (Srivastava et al. 2024).
}
\section{Workflow}{

\enumerate{
\item \code{\link[=as_scmp]{as_scmp()}} or \code{\link[=create_scmp]{create_scmp()}}: a \link[=ScMaSigPro-class]{ScMaSigPro} object from the
counts and one pseudotime value and one path label per cell.
\item \code{\link[=sc.squeeze]{sc.squeeze()}}: pseudotime bins and pseudo-bulk counts for each path;
\code{\link[=sc.restruct]{sc.restruct()}} adds the bins of a shared root to every path.
\item \code{\link[=sc.set.poly]{sc.set.poly()}}: the polynomial design.
\item \code{\link[=sc.p.vector]{sc.p.vector()}}: the test of each gene's full model, which selects the
genes with a non-flat profile.
\item \code{\link[=sc.t.fit]{sc.t.fit()}}: stepwise selection of the significant terms of each of
these genes.
\item \code{\link[=sc.filter]{sc.filter()}}: lists of significant genes; \code{\link[=sc.cluster.trend]{sc.cluster.trend()}}
clusters them.
\item \code{\link[=plotTrend]{plotTrend()}}, \code{\link[=plotTrendCluster]{plotTrendCluster()}}, \code{\link[=plotIntersect]{plotIntersect()}}: plots;
\code{\link[=scmpResults]{scmpResults()}}: the results as a table with one row per gene.
}
}

\section{Input}{

The workflow needs one pseudotime value and one path label per cell.
\code{\link[=assign_paths]{assign_paths()}} and \code{\link[=paths_from_graph]{paths_from_graph()}} build them from the lineage
weights or the graph of a trajectory tool; the "Input contract" section
of \code{\link[=assign_paths]{assign_paths()}} describes the format.
}

